.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQKSEAL 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqkseal ,
.Nm nqkopen
.Nd seal one message to an ML-KEM public key
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqkseal
.Fa "nqkalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqkopen
.Fa "nqkalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *in" "size_t n"
.Fa "uint8_t *msg" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqkseal
encrypts the
.Fa n
bytes at
.Fa msg
so that only the holder of the secret key of
.Fa pk
can read them, and
.Fn nqkopen
reads them back.
It exists for one use, the hidden list of a commitment, and does
nothing more: one recipient, one message, no padding.
.Fa alg
is
.Dv NQMLKEM512 ,
.Dv NQMLKEM768
or
.Dv NQMLKEM1024 .
.Pp
The format, noqtis-kseal-1, is fixed:
.Bl -column "ML-KEM ciphertext" "the KEM's size" -offset indent
.It Sy field Ta Sy bytes
.It Li NQKS Ta 4
.It version, 1 Ta 1
.It Fa alg Ta 1
.It ML-KEM ciphertext Ta 768, 1088 or 1568
.It ciphertext of Fa msg Ta Fa n
.It tag Ta 16
.El
.Pp
A fresh ML-KEM encapsulation to
.Fa pk
gives a 32-byte shared secret.
HKDF-SHA-256 of it (no salt), with info the string
.Li noqtis-kseal-1 ,
the SHA3-256 of
.Fa pk ,
the context's length (one byte) and bytes, the 6-byte header and the KEM
ciphertext, gives the 32-byte key and 12-byte nonce of
ChaCha20-Poly1305, whose associated data is the header, the KEM
ciphertext and the context's length and bytes.
The context
.Fa ctx
(at most 255 bytes;
.Dv NULL
with 0 for none) names what the message is for and must be given again
to open it.
.Pp
The output of
.Fn nqkseal
is
.Dv NQKSOVH
(22) plus the KEM ciphertext plus
.Fa n
bytes, with
.Fa n
at most
.Dv NQKSMAX
(2^30);
.Pf * Fa outlen
gets it, also when
.Fa cap
is too small.
.Fn nqkopen
writes the message to
.Fa msg
(cap bytes) and its size to
.Pf * Fa outlen .
Every changed byte, another key, another set or another context is
refused: ML-KEM's implicit rejection turns a changed KEM ciphertext or
another key into another shared secret, and the tag fails.
On any error the message buffer is zeroed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
pointer with a nonzero length, a context over 255 bytes, an unknown
.Fa alg .
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
A key of the wrong length or a secret key that ML-KEM refuses; for
.Fn nqkopen ,
an input that is not noqtis-kseal-1 for
.Fa alg
or is shorter than its header, KEM ciphertext and tag.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
The tag does not verify.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
.Fa n
is over
.Dv NQKSMAX .
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fa alg
is HQC.
.It Bq Er NQERNG
The random source failed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqenc 3 ,
.Xr nqrand 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 203 (ML-KEM), RFC 5869 (HKDF), RFC 8439 (ChaCha20-Poly1305).
